  "text": "Audioscripts\nUntil the 19th century, soap was regarded asa luxury item, and was heavily taxed in\nseveral countries. As it became more readily available, it became an everyday necessity, a\ndevelopment that was reinforced when the high tax was removed. Soap was then something\nQ40\nordinary people could afford, and cleanliness standards improved.\nWith this widespread use came the development of milder soaps for bathing and soaps for use\nin the washing machines that were available to consumers by the turn of the 20th century.\n112\n",
